From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 00:35:16 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8015-d221: Let the Wi-Fi firmware follow
 the country

Apple's Broadcom firmware starts in the NVRAM's worldwide locale (XZ),
and in it refuses joins on most 5 GHz channels at once, with nothing
sent: brcmfmac reports status 16 within about 100 ms. brcmfmac passes
the regulatory country (from an access point's country element, or
user space) to the firmware only when the node says how to translate
it. Use the trivial map, as the iPad 5 already does: Apple's CLM takes
the ISO 3166 code with revision 0.

On a J71b among access points that announce ID, joins on 5 GHz failed
until a firmware reload while channel 6 worked; with the firmware's
country set to ID, reconnects on channel 153 succeeded every time.
This covers the iPhone X (D221).

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8015-d221.dts | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8015-d221.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8015-d221.dts
index c2c8486fdfc5..4abebf4ff9ba 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8015-d221.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8015-d221.dts
@@ -36,5 +36,6 @@ wifi0: wifi@0,0 {
 		reg = <0x10000 0x0 0x0 0x0 0x0>;
 		device-wake-gpios = <&pinctrl_ap 40 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
 		vdd-supply = <&wlan_vdd>;
+		brcm,ccode-map-trivial;
 	};
 };
